//! OpenGL ES 1.1 tokens and types — the names the specification is written in.
//!
//! **Generated. DO NOT EDIT.** Regenerate with:
//!
//!     python3 scripts/gl/es11_enums.py > src/drivers/gl/es/enums.zig
//!
//! Read out of the Khronos OpenGL ES 1.1 header (GLES/gl.h) (the Khronos header, generated in turn from
//! the Khronos XML API registry). The specification prose never states these numbers;
//! the header is the only place they exist, so it is the only honest source for them.
//!
//! These are the values that cross the API boundary — what an application passes to
//! glEnable or glTexParameteri. They are NOT how state is stored: everything inside
//! this module works in real Zig enums and structs, and a token is mapped to one at
//! the entry point, once, where an unknown token becomes GL_INVALID_ENUM. A GLenum
//! reaching any deeper than that is a bug.

